WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.131
An Indian spacecraft reached the Moon in

2
00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:04.023
twenty nineteen and was meant to work

3
00:00:04.023 --> 00:00:05.509
for one year.

4
00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:07.425
ISRO now expects it to last about

5
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:08.398
seven.

6
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:11.561
It launched in July twenty nineteen.

7
00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:12.815
The lander, Vikram,

8
00:00:12.815 --> 00:00:14.475
separated in September,

9
00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:16.472
but crashed four days later after a

10
00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:17.782
software glitch.

11
00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:20.493
NASA's own Moon orbiter later photographed the

12
00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:22.734
spot where Vikram came down.

13
00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:23.558
The Indian orbiter,

14
00:00:23.558 --> 00:00:25.124
though, carried on.

15
00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.869
It circles the Moon over the poles,

16
00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:29.553
about a hundred kilometres up,

17
00:00:29.553 --> 00:00:31.433
with eight instruments.

18
00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:33.384
Its camera can see details as small

19
00:00:33.384 --> 00:00:35.158
as thirty centimetres.

20
00:00:35.558 --> 00:00:37.915
It has mapped sodium on the surface,

21
00:00:37.915 --> 00:00:41.224
detected argon-forty in the Moon's thin atmosphere,

22
00:00:41.224 --> 00:00:43.418
found chromium and manganese,

23
00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.241
and watched a large solar flare in

24
00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:46.632
twenty twenty-four.

25
00:00:47.032 --> 00:00:49.145
In twenty twenty-three it also served as

26
00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:51.790
a communication relay for Chandrayaan-3.

27
00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.061
For GS Three,

28
00:00:53.061 --> 00:00:54.976
remember this: a mission can miss one

29
00:00:54.976 --> 00:00:57.738
goal and still deliver years of science.

